There are N points on the xy-plane numbered 1, 2, …, N, where the coordinates of point i are (i, A_i). For each i = 1, 2, …, N−1, draw a line segment connecting point i to point i+1 to form a single polyline. Determine the number of points on this polyline (including the endpoints) whose y-coordinate is K. Note that, given the constraints, it is guaranteed that the number of points satisfying the condition is finite.
Constraints
2 ≤ N ≤ 100
1 ≤ A_i ≤ 100 (1 ≤ i ≤ N)
A_i ≠ A_(i+1) (1 ≤ i < N)
1 ≤ K ≤ 100
All input values are integers.
Input
The input is provided via standard input in the following format:
N K
A_1 A_2 ~ A_N
Output
Output the number of points on the broken line whose y-coordinate is K.
